t/ui/test_ui.c, t/ui/test_graph.c, t/shell/test_shell.c, t/ui/test_kbd.c, t/loop/test_loop_native.c:539, t/assistant/test_binding.c and t/assistant/test_view.c set d.scale = 100 as a literal in their fixtures, while include/canlin/ui_limits.h names the step as CANLIN_UI_SCALE_STEP_100. The fixtures should read the constant, so a change of the steps does not leave the tests asserting a stale number. Found by the 2026-11-14 work on k110.
